    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "fa6e5ce4-8158-4dd0-a32c-5dd9729c774a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the closed ball {v : d(c, v) <= r} of radius r about c; today a scene token \
only"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"08593b9c-7ccf-4230-a8ad-f0f54fd34ab8"],

Cell["waits: InfraTube, the tube of radius s about a core", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"13d50404-95c5-4055-bcf1-5e2a1f1cff1b"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraCone, the cone of a given slope with apex at one end of an axis\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f02a368d-d8a0-40d5-99c4-80408f8e4df6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraAngle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraAngle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "51148256-b8a9-4681-8ecb-ea983c66df9f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the angle at p between q1 and q2 in radians, Method \"Arclength\" or \
\"Alexandrov\", the comparison angle of the three distances; a method from \
the shortest paths waits"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9bda3490-1c87-40fa-850a-accc42e0820b"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraCrossection, an invariant of four points, as the distance is of \
two points and the angle of three\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"da7896e4-6f8e-45ed-ba5f-950f0c9790d5"]
}, Open  ]],

